# Every env file is a secret until proven otherwise, and the proof is being an
# example. Firebase also reads functions/.env.<project-id>, which is the one
# that would have slipped through: a file with real keys, one deploy away from a
# public repository.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.emulator.example
!.env.test
functions/.env*
!functions/.env.example

